## 10. Functional Requirements

### 10.1 Product Framework

> Methodology: define the deployment process, its evidence and failure states before choosing scripts or integrations. Diagrams show a logical design, not a claim of implemented features.

#### Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
 subgraph UserLayer["User layer"]
  Tech[IT Support]
 end
 subgraph AccessLayer["Access layer"]
  Admin[Authorized management access]
 end
 subgraph ServiceLayer["Service layer"]
  FOG[FOG<br/>Images and deployment tasks]
  Prep[Validated Windows automation<br/>Naming and setup]
  Gate[Readiness checks<br/>Stage results]
 end
 subgraph DataLayer["Data layer"]
  Images[(Versioned images)]
  Records[(Task records and logs)]
  Backup[(External backup<br/>Current and previous generation)]
 end
 subgraph ExternalSystems["External systems"]
  Network[Approved DHCP and boot network]
  Entra[Entra identity and recovery keys]
  Apps[Activation and agent services]
  Device[Dell endpoints]
 end
 Tech --> Admin --> FOG
 FOG --> Images
 FOG --> Records
 Network -.-> Device
 FOG --> Device --> Prep --> Gate
 Prep -.-> Entra
 Prep -.-> Apps
 Gate --> Records
 Images --> Backup
 Records --> Backup
```

| Boundary | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| FOG and boot network | Transfer approved images only to authorized target devices |
| Windows automation | Resume across restarts, record results, use verified integration methods |
| Entra / vendors | External identity, activation and recovery association; permissions required |
| Backup | Recover images plus the configuration and metadata required to use them |

#### Logical data model

```mermaid
erDiagram
 DEVICE ||--o{ DEPLOYMENT : receives
 IMAGE_VERSION ||--o{ DEPLOYMENT : supplies
 DEPLOYMENT ||--o{ STAGE_RESULT : records
 DEVICE ||--o{ NAME_RESERVATION : has
 BACKUP_SET ||--o{ BACKUP_ITEM : contains
 IMAGE_VERSION ||--o{ BACKUP_ITEM : copied_as
 DEVICE {
  string service_tag PK
  string model
  string entra_device_id
 }
 IMAGE_VERSION {
  string image_version_id PK
  string model
  string office_variant
  string checksum
  string status
 }
 DEPLOYMENT {
  string deployment_id PK
  string service_tag FK
  string image_version_id FK
  string technician_id
  string approved_name
  string status
 }
 STAGE_RESULT {
  string result_id PK
  string deployment_id FK
  string stage
  string start_time
  string end_time
  string result
 }
 NAME_RESERVATION {
  string normalized_name PK
  string service_tag FK
  string status
 }
 BACKUP_SET {
  string backup_id PK
  string generation
  string verification_status
 }
 BACKUP_ITEM {
  string backup_item_id PK
  string backup_id FK
  string image_version_id FK
  string checksum
 }
```

| Entity | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Device | Service Tag anchors identity; a reused USB adapter's MAC address alone is insufficient |
| Image version | Immutable approved version; model and Office variant explicit |
| Deployment / stage result | Each attempt preserved; retries do not erase failed-attempt history |
| Name reservation | Case-insensitive unique active name; release/reuse explicitly reviewed |
| Backup set / item | Manifest identifies six image versions and matching recoverable configuration |

These are logical records. Reuse native FOG data and a small protected supplementary record store as needed; no new database product is mandated.

#### Deployment process

```mermaid
flowchart TD
 A[Preflight and Service Tag check] --> B{Reused device?}
 B -->|Yes| C[Verify employee backup<br/>Authorize approved erasure]
 B -->|No| D[Select model and Office image]
 C --> D
 D --> E[Validate and reserve name<br/>Approve any adjustment]
 E --> F[Start deployment clock<br/>Secure Boot network boot]
 F --> G[Restore approved image]
 G --> H[First boot and device-specific setup]
 H --> I[Supported Entra join<br/>Apps, activation and updates]
 I --> J[Complete encryption<br/>Verify recovery association]
 J --> K{All required checks pass?}
 K -->|Yes| L[Ready for validation<br/>Stop deployment clock]
 K -->|No| X[Blocked<br/>Record fault and remediation]
 X --> H
 L --> M[Separate technician sign-in and tests]
 M --> N{Tests pass?}
 N -->|Yes| O[Approved for handoff]
 N -->|No| X
 style F fill:#dceeff
 style L fill:#dff0d8
 style O fill:#dff0d8
 style X fill:#ffd9d9
```

| Stage group | Clock / owner |
| --- | --- |
| Preflight | Separate; technician |
| Imaging through readiness | Deployment; automation plus any recorded interventions |
| Sign-in and functional validation | Separate technician clock |
| Remediation | Separately identified and included in total completion reporting |

#### State machine

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
 [*] --> Preflight
 Preflight --> Approved: identity and prerequisites checked
 Approved --> Deploying: technician starts
 Deploying --> Configuring: image restored
 Configuring --> Encrypting: setup and join complete
 Encrypting --> ReadyForValidation: encryption and evidence pass
 ReadyForValidation --> Validating: technician signs in
 Validating --> Accepted: all tests pass
 Deploying --> Blocked: transfer failure
 Configuring --> Blocked: setup or identity failure
 Encrypting --> Blocked: protection or escrow failure
 Validating --> Blocked: functional test failure
 Blocked --> Configuring: approved safe retry
 Blocked --> Preflight: reimage required
 Accepted --> [*]
 note right of ReadyForValidation
  Encryption underway is insufficient.
  No handoff before separate validation.
 end note
```

| Transition | Control |
| --- | --- |
| Preflight → Approved | Correct device, image, name, backup and erasure checks |
| Blocked → retry | Owner identifies safe restart point; no blind rerun of identity creation |
| Encrypting → Ready | Encryption complete, protection active, correct recovery association verified |
| Validating → Accepted | Technician checklist and elapsed time recorded |

#### Operator surfaces

| Surface | Required actions |
| --- | --- |
| Image catalog | Filter model / Office / version / status; view approval and test evidence |
| Deployment selection | Enter Service Tag, employee/name and image; confirm target disk and prerequisites |
| Task status | View stages, timings, failures and readiness; request approved retry |
| Maintenance records | Promote images, verify backup manifest, record restore test |
| Implementation | Existing FOG UI plus approved companion scripts/checklists; no mobile app requirement |

### 10.2 Requirement Details

#### Image catalog and capture

Process: prepare clean reference → patch/configure → generalize → capture → test → approve → publish.

| Image family | Office 2016 variant | Microsoft 365 variant |
| --- | --- | --- |
| DC15250 | DC15250-O2016 | DC15250-M365 |
| DC16250 | DC16250-O2016 | DC16250-M365 |
| ECS1250 | ECS1250-O2016 | ECS1250-M365 |

Version suffix proposal: YYYY-MM plus revision. Track Windows build, drivers, application versions, capture date, checksum, approval and test results.

- **IMG-01 (constraint):** Technician selects only an approved compatible model/Office image. Detect mismatches before destructive work.
- **IMG-02 (constraint):** Reference images must be generalized and unjoined; exclude employee data, tenant enrollment tokens, device recovery keys and copied registered-agent identities.
- **IMG-03 (constraint):** Windows/Office activation and Webroot/Resolve preparation must follow verified licensing and vendor deployment methods. Preinstalled software is not proof of a unique valid activation.
- **IMG-04 (trigger):** Refresh all six images monthly; test both variants per model before promotion. Do not automatically publish an untested candidate.
- **IMG-05 (constraint):** Standard software includes correct Office variant, Chrome, Acrobat Reader, Zoom Workplace, Teams, Webroot, Resolve and applicable StarTech drivers. Install/stage location is determined by supported imaging practice. Remove conflicting Office packages.

#### Boot, target identification and deployment

Process: identify hardware → authorize task → network boot → image → verify startup.

Operator fields: Service Tag, detected model, target disk, adapter identifier, selected image version, proposed name, employee assignment reference, backup/erasure status and initiating technician.

- **DEP-01:** Preserve Secure Boot throughout. Validate signed boot chain and certificate-enrollment procedure on each model and adapter.
- **DEP-02:** Prove exact FOG release compatibility with Ubuntu 26.04.1 and firmware before rollout. A version change requires a documented decision.
- **DEP-03:** Use approved DHCP/boot configuration. Do not introduce competing office DHCP service or automatic destructive default boot.
- **DEP-04:** Group multicast tasks only for compatible devices receiving the same image. Pilot same-image and mixed-image scheduling; do not promise 14 arbitrary images at unlimited speed.
- **DEP-05:** Associate tasks with Service Tags and verify actual hardware when adapters move between laptops.
- **DEP-06:** For returned equipment, verify the preserved backup and authorize the appropriate erasure/reprovisioning method before writing. Reimaging alone is not proof that all recoverable old disk data has been sanitized.

#### Naming

Process: enter employee and type → propose name → validate → check/reserve → technician approves changes → apply before enrollment.

- **NAM-01:** Format LPT-{employee token}-LPT or LPT-{employee token}-PC, uppercase, maximum 15 characters.
- **NAM-02 (proposed):** Start with first initial plus surname. Laptop token budget is 7 characters; desktop token budget is 8. Strip unsupported characters under a documented normalization rule. Preserve the user's original input in the review record.
- **NAM-03 (proposed):** For long names, propose initial plus truncated surname; always request technician approval. For collisions, propose a truncated token plus a numeric suffix within the same budget; never silently rename.
- **NAM-04 (proposed):** If retaining the existing NEW replacement convention, reserve three token characters for NEW, truncate the employee token as necessary and request approval. A collision suffix must also fit the budget. Previous approved device records remain intact until reviewed.
- **NAM-05:** Check active FOG names and current deployment reservations case-insensitively. Serialize reservation creation so concurrent tasks cannot claim one name.
- **NAM-06:** Authorized Entra lookup is preferred for existing fleet conflicts. Device display names are not unique identifiers; associate matches with device IDs. Do not delete stale objects automatically or treat lookup failure as “available.”
- **NAM-07:** If directory lookup cannot be authorized, show “directory duplicate check unavailable” and require technician verification. Do not claim fleet-wide uniqueness from local records alone.

#### Entra joining and Windows setup

Process: apply name → provision unique join → confirm tenant/device identity → perform dependent configuration → report.

- **AUT-01:** Investigate PowerShell-triggered provisioning using a supported method. Applying a package is an orchestration step, not a replacement for entitlement, token, tenant or role prerequisites.
- **AUT-02:** Demonstrate unattended join on a freshly imaged pilot and after reimaging that same hardware; verify that other devices are unaffected.
- **AUT-03:** Keep reusable enrollment material out of base images and ordinary logs; define secure distribution, expiry/renewal and revocation if the selected method uses it.
- **AUT-04:** If existing-license automation fails feasibility, stop architectural commitment and obtain a stakeholder decision. Manual joining is not silently accepted.
- **AUT-05:** Employee accounts remain standard. Technician/service privileges must not become employee privileges.
- **AUT-06:** Install/register Teams, Resolve, Webroot and other required software using validated methods; verify unique records and correct versions.
- **AUT-07:** Run approved cleanup and Windows/driver/Microsoft-product update workflow, with bounded retries and restart checkpoints. Do not call a device ready while approved required updates or reboots remain unresolved. The approved update set and firmware scope are O4.
- **AUT-08:** Scripts must resume safely after reboot and report partial failure. Verification must distinguish software installed from activation/registration successful. Microsoft 365 user sign-in is separately handled.

#### BitLocker readiness

Process: establish unique device identity → configure approved encryption/protectors → escrow recovery material → wait for completion → verify association.

- **SEC-01:** The OS volume and any approved employee-data volumes must finish encryption; 100% conversion alone must not conceal protection being suspended or disabled.
- **SEC-02:** Require active protection and a device-specific recovery protector correctly associated with that device in Entra before Ready for validation.
- **SEC-03:** Log status, protector/key identifier and verification outcome, never the recovery password. Scope any directory/recovery read permissions to approved roles.
- **SEC-04:** Proposed baseline is full-volume encryption, including free space, particularly for reused devices. Stakeholder explicitly requires completion; precise cipher, protector and full-volume/used-space policy remains O5. Never choose used-space-only just to meet timing without approval.
- **SEC-05:** Pilot recovery-key retrieval and recovery on authorized test equipment; do not force a recovery event on every production deployment.

#### Backup and image lifecycle

Process: build candidate → validate → promote → copy and verify → retain preceding approved generation → retire older generation.

- **BKP-01:** Separate external drive, believed 8 TB; verify actual available capacity. At steady state retain six current and six previous-month image versions, plus matching configuration/metadata.
- **BKP-02:** Back up database/configuration, image definitions, automation, version manifests and necessary boot trust material with appropriate access protection. Image files alone are insufficient.
- **BKP-03:** Verify copy integrity and a usable restore procedure. During rotation, temporary staging may require more than 12 files; do not remove the last verified fallback before the replacement is valid.
- **BKP-04:** Previous-generation recovery must preserve matching image metadata and avoid unintentionally restoring stale deployment/identity records.
- **BKP-05:** Monthly backup implies up to approximately a month of unbacked configuration change. Proposed additional configuration backup after material changes; Director to decide in O6.

### 10.3 Exception Handling

| Scenario | Required response |
| --- | --- |
| Transfer/network interruption | Mark failed; retain evidence; technician authorizes safe restart/reimage |
| Enrollment/token expired | Block readiness; owner renews or repairs supported mechanism; prevent duplicate identity creation |
| Name collision / concurrent reservation | Reject conflicting reservation and request technician-approved alternative |
| Directory lookup unavailable | Report unknown; bounded retry or explicit manual verification |
| Wrong image / disk selection | Prevent start when detected; require preflight again after cancellation |
| Missing/corrupt employee backup | Block erasure and deployment |
| Activation/agent failure | Block corresponding completion gate; do not overwrite another device record |
| Encryption slow or escrow mismatch | Continue measuring elapsed time, flag target breach; never mark ready early |
| Update reboot loop | Stop after validated retry limit; surface logs and unresolved update |
| Corrupt new image / backup full | Retain previous verified generation; investigate; do not rotate blindly |
| Staff approval delayed | Keep pending and escalate to owner; no automatic destructive approval |

## 11. Data Tracking

Use local deployment logs and an approved summary record; external analytics are not required. Record operator, device Service Tag, deployment ID, image version, stage, timestamp, result and error code. Never record passwords, license keys, recovery secrets or enrollment tokens.

| Event | Evidence / purpose |
| --- | --- |
| Catalog/task/status accessed | Operational audit if supported; do not build an analytics subsystem just for page views |
| Task approved / started | Who authorized which hardware, image and name |
| Stage started / finished / failed | Transfer, setup, join, apps, updates, encryption and readiness timings |
| Name reserved / adjusted | Original proposal, approved result and approving technician |
| Ready for validation | Complete machine-side acceptance evidence |
| Validation started / finished | Separate technician effort, elapsed time and pass/fail checklist |
| Image promoted / backup verified | Version, checksum, approval and restore evidence |

Report single-device and batch elapsed time, first-pass success, failure/retry count, hands-on effort and identity incidents. Compare image-transfer performance to the 3–4-hour transfer baseline; do not compare total new deployment time to old transfer time as a like-for-like percentage. Show sample counts and failures. [TODO O9: log retention and reporting interval.]

