| IT Support operator | Select approved image, approve name adjustment, authorize assigned-device task after preflight, validate and record handoff |
| Maintenance owner | Maintain service/scripts, prepare/test/promote images, backup/restore, investigate failures |
| Director of IT | Approve network production rollout, unresolved policy choices, changed scope/budget and release disposition |
| Network administrator | Approve/configure DHCP, VLAN, routing and multicast settings |
| Tenant administrator | Approve tenant method/permissions and manage enrollment/recovery access |
| Employee | Standard Windows user; no FOG or deployment administrative access |

Use named authorized access where supported. Match logical roles to actual FOG capabilities; do not assume fine-grained native RBAC exists. Limit server/console access and approved scripts where native controls are insufficient.

Read-only name lookup should use least-privilege authorized directory access. Name lookup does not authorize deletion of device records or retrieval of recovery secrets. Protect backup access and signing material. Keep tenant credentials and product keys outside shared images and ordinary logs. [TODO O2/O6: assign tenant permissions, backup protection and secret-storage mechanism.]

## 13. Operations Plan

Proposed schedule, subject to pilot findings and staff availability:

| Phase | Target window | Exit evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Discovery and feasibility | Early October 2026 | Network inventory; exact boot compatibility; enrollment method proof |
| Six images and automation | First half of October | Generalized references; validated applications and restart handling |
| Model and batch pilot | Mid-October | Six variant tests, representative batch timings and security checks |
| Backup recovery / staff training | Late October | Verified restore exercise; operator competency |
| Production decision | Before November 1 | Director accepts evidence and outstanding dispositions |

Review network placement before production connection changes. Prefer a controlled deployment segment if existing infrastructure permits; topology is not yet approved.

Monthly procedure: refresh six candidates, test both Office variants on each model, approve/publish, update current/previous external backup, verify integrity and review deployment failures. Record actual maintenance effort. Employee archival backups remain separate; retention policy is O6.

Clonezilla is intended to be phased out. Proposed retirement gate: successful pilot, demonstrated recovery from the FOG backup and Director approval. Until then retain the existing recovery option; do not destroy its media as part of this documentation task.

Deliverables:
1. This PRD and decision log.
2. Version-specific technician runbook, currently a pilot draft.
3. Training guide and hands-on competency checklist.
4. During implementation: tested scripts/configuration, six approved images, deployment evidence and backup/restore evidence.

No training session or implementation has yet been performed. The supplied runbook and training guide must be finalized against the selected FOG release and demonstrated workflow.

Post-launch review proposal: review the first month of deployments for adoption, timing, failures, identity correctness and maintenance load; adjust only through recorded decisions.

