## Appendix A: Acceptance Checklist

| Test | Pass condition |
| --- | --- |
| Six-image coverage | Each model × Office combination boots and passes app/driver checks |
| Secure Boot | Remains enabled through network boot, deployment and normal startup |
| Name validation | Long names blocked/reviewed; duplicate reservation rejected; NEW fits limit; lookup outage never reports false availability |
| Entra / agents | Correct tenant and distinct identities; redeploy does not overwrite another endpoint |
| Permissions | Employee is standard; deployment secrets absent from employee-accessible artifacts/logs |
| BitLocker | Approved encryption complete; protection active; correct key association verified; pilot recovery test succeeds |
| Updates / cleanup | Approved scripts complete; required updates/reboots resolved; approved app/startup baseline met |
| Timing | Separate preflight, deployment, batch and technician clocks; full encryption inside deployment; failures retained |
| Interrupted tasks | Transfer, network, reboot and enrollment failures visible with safe recovery |
| Reuse | Employee backup verified; approved erasure documented; no former employee profile/data in deployed environment |
| Backup | Six current and six previous images with matching configuration; checksums and restore exercise pass |
| Release | Runbook finalized, training passed, open release decisions resolved, Director approval recorded |

## Appendix B: Self-Check and To-Be-Completed List

| Review dimension | Assessment |
| --- | --- |
| Business analysis / positioning | Concrete workload and constraints; labor baseline remains O9 |
| Product adaptation | Internal service; no sales/market-size or SaaS requirements |
| Scenarios and structure | New device, reuse and monthly refresh; all 14 chapters present |
| Architecture and data | Logical diagrams provided; implementation remains pilot work |
| Process, roles and interactions | Explicit operator fields, ownership, gates and failure handling |
| Cost-benefit | Existing assets documented; ROI not fabricated |
| MVP and evolution | Six-image workflow in scope; integrations deferred |
| Robustness | Identity, network, data-loss and backup exceptions addressed |
| AI features / multi-tenancy | Not applicable |
| Operations and tracking | Training, maintenance, retirement and stage timing defined |
| Main unresolved risk | Supported automated joining within current entitlements, secure boot compatibility and measured performance |

**Must resolve before production:** O1–O5 and O8, plus backup recoverability in O6. These establish that deployment can work, preserves identity/security, and has a credible performance commitment.

**Must resolve before operational sign-off:** naming policy O7, complete backup/retention choices O6, and technician timing/maintenance/log choices O9.

**Optional future refinement:** SharePoint assignment lookup/writeback, CSV-assisted batch input, additional hardware families and expanded reporting. None is a release-one dependency.

A full PRD review can follow once the critical evidence is supplied; this draft's self-check is not a production approval.

